 "response": "Tepi's budget now is **$1,525K**. This is a long hand calculation; I double-checked each step, but some risk of slips remains.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office budget updates count. Other teams' messages and non-budget Finance notes (audits, invoices, room changes) were ignored.\n2. I traced each chain of withdrawals from the most recent link backwards. Each withdrawal cancels the item it points to, unless that withdrawal has itself been withdrawn.\n3. I applied every remaining budget update in order, starting from the $1,810K set in #0001.\n\n**Example withdrawal chains**\n- **#0002 (\u2212$138K):** #1545 withdraws #0504, which revives #0031, which cancels #0018, which revives #0005. #0005 withdraws #0002, so the decrease does not apply.\n- **#0036 (+$243K):** #0290 cancels #0142, which revives #0064, which cancels #0055. Nothing withdraws #0036 any more, so the increase applies.\n- **#0035 (+$593K):** #0920 is the last link in a long chain back through #0331, #0119, #0084 and #0069. The net effect is that #0035 stands, so the increase applies.\n\n**Running total at a few points**\n\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0003 | $1,735K |\n| #0597 | $562K |\n| #0666 | $1,756K |\n| #1250 | $2,095K |\n| #1596 (last budget change) | $1,525K |\n\nANSWER: $1525K",
